{
	"info": {
		"name": "Yam API — Appel Audio (avec auth Sanctum)",
		"description": "Collection Postman pour l'API Yam (appels audio WebRTC).\n\nURL de production : https://yam.mdkrlabs.dev\n\nCommence par « 0. Login » avec ton numéro et ton mot de passe Yam. La réponse contient data.token ; Postman le stocke automatiquement et l'envoie ensuite dans Authorization: Bearer <token>.\n\nLes clés des corps POST sont préremplies dans Body > form-data ; renseigne les valeurs avant l'envoi. Pour les signaux WebRTC, les champs imbriqués payload[sdp][type] et payload[sdp][sdp] sont interprétés par Laravel comme un objet payload.\n\nCette API n'expose pas le chemin /api/web/v1/users/connecte_useraccount : l'authentification se fait sur /api/v1/auth/login, et le profil sur /api/v1/users/me.\n\nLes endpoints d'appels agissent sur de vrais appareils : vérifie les identifiants cible avant de les envoyer.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{
			"key": "base_url",
			"value": "https://yam.mdkrlabs.dev",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "device_id",
			"value": "test-123",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "tokenApprovisionne",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "tokenMedecin",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		},
		{
			"key": "tokenPatient",
			"value": "",
			"type": "string"
		}
	],
	"auth": {
		"type": "bearer",
		"bearer": [
			{
				"key": "token",
				"value": "{{tokenApprovisionne}}",
				"type": "string"
			}
		]
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "0. Login — obtenir le token Bearer",
			"request": {
				"method": "POST",
				"header": [
					{
						"key": "Accept",
						"value": "application/json"
					}
				],
				"auth": {
					"type": "noauth"
				},
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/login",
					"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
					"path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
				},
				"body": {
					"mode": "formdata",
					"formdata": [
						{"key": "phone_number", "value": "", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "password", "value": "", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "device_id", "value": "{{device_id}}", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "platform", "value": "web", "type": "text", "enabled": true}
					]
				},
				"description": "Renseigne phone_number et password avec les identifiants d'un compte Yam existant, puis envoie cette requête. Le token Sanctum de la réponse data.token est enregistré automatiquement dans la variable de collection tokenApprovisionne. N'utilise pas de compte de démonstration en production."
			},
			"response": [],
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"pm.test('Login réussi (HTTP 200)', function() {",
							"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
							"});",
							"const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
							"pm.test('La réponse contient un token Sanctum', function() {",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData.data.token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
							"});",
							"pm.collectionVariables.set('tokenApprovisionne', jsonData.data.token);"
						]
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "1. Get Contacts",
			"request": {
				"method": "GET",
				"header": [
					{
						"key": "Accept",
						"value": "application/json"
					}
				],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/contacts",
					"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
					"path": ["api", "v1", "contacts"]
				},
				"description": "Liste les contacts visibles par l'utilisateur connecté. Nécessite le token Bearer obtenu avec « 0. Login »."
			},
			"response": [],
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
							"pm.test('Réponse contient contacts', function() {",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('contacts');",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData.contacts).to.be.an('array');",
							"});",
							"",
							"if (jsonData.contacts && jsonData.contacts.length > 0) {",
							"    var first = jsonData.contacts[0];",
							"    pm.collectionVariables.set('target_user_id', first.user_id);",
							"    pm.collectionVariables.set('target_device_id', first.device_id || 'unknown');",
							"    pm.collectionVariables.set('target_username', first.username);",
							"    console.log('✅ ' + jsonData.contacts.length + ' contact(s) trouvé(s)');",
							"    console.log('   Premier : ' + first.username + ' (device: ' + (first.device_id || 'N/A') + ')');",
							"    console.log('   → target_device_id mis à jour');",
							"} else {",
							"    console.log('⚠️ Aucun contact trouvé');",
							"}"
						]
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "2. Ring (Appel entrant)",
			"request": {
				"method": "POST",
				"header": [
					{
						"key": "Accept",
						"value": "application/json"
					}
				],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/call/ring",
					"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
					"path": ["api", "v1", "call", "ring"]
				},
				"body": {
					"mode": "formdata",
					"formdata": [
						{"key": "to_device_id", "value": "", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "to_phone_number", "value": "", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "from_device_id", "value": "{{device_id}}", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "from_username", "value": "", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "type", "value": "audio", "type": "text", "enabled": true}
					]
				},
				"description": "Déclenche une sonnerie sur l'appareil ciblé. Nécessite le token Bearer. Le device_id cible doit correspondre à un appareil connecté ; adapte les champs JSON avant l'envoi."
			},
			"response": [],
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
							"pm.test('Ring envoyé', function() {",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData.ok).to.be.true;",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('call_id');",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData.call_id).to.not.be.empty;",
							"});",
							"pm.collectionVariables.set('call_id', jsonData.call_id);",
							"console.log('✅ Call ID : ' + jsonData.call_id);",
							"console.log('   → Le client connecté au canal device.' + pm.variables.get('device_id') + ' devrait sonner !');"
						]
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "3. WebRTC Signal",
			"request": {
				"method": "POST",
				"header": [
					{
						"key": "Accept",
						"value": "application/json"
					}
				],
				"url": {
					"raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/call/signal",
					"host": ["{{base_url}}"],
					"path": ["api", "v1", "call", "signal"]
				},
				"body": {
					"mode": "formdata",
					"formdata": [
						{"key": "to_device_id", "value": "", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "to_user_id", "value": "", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "from_device_id", "value": "{{device_id}}", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "type", "value": "offer", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "payload[sdp][type]", "value": "offer", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "payload[sdp][sdp]", "value": "", "type": "text", "enabled": true},
						{"key": "call_id", "value": "", "type": "text", "enabled": true}
					]
				},
				"description": "Envoie un message de signaling WebRTC au device ciblé. Nécessite le token Bearer. Types : offer, answer ou candidate. Remplace les valeurs d'exemple dans le corps JSON par les données SDP/ICE de l'appel."
			},
			"response": [],
			"event": [
				{
					"listen": "test",
					"script": {
						"type": "text/javascript",
						"exec": [
							"var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
							"pm.test('Signal diffusé', function() {",
							"    pm.expect(jsonData.ok).to.be.true;",
							"});",
							"console.log('✅ Signal envoyé au device : ' + pm.collectionVariables.get('device_id'));"
						]
					}
				}
			]
		}
	]
}
